On Tuesday, the 9th of March, Peter H. thusly spake:

> Hi,
> 
> I have been spam free for the past 6 months. Now all of a sudden I get regular 
> spam by apparently a subscriber this list linux-newbie.
> 
> Is it only me since I see no one else is complaining?
> 
> Can it be stopped at the source that is at linux-newbie?
> 
> What information is needed? The spam comes with hostname constantly changing 
> in the Message-Id:, however, not the ISP itself.
> 
> Regards

linux-newbie is archived publicly on the net, for example at
groups.google.com and address-harvester can easily pick up any one
subscribers email address.
Chances are, your spam comes from this.

If the spammer really always uses the same ISP to sent their junk, 
the usual way would be to complain to abuse@isp.com (or other 
contact address for example taken from a whois lookup).

